story += [tbl([[P(v,'thx') for v in cc[0]]]+[[P(v,'tinyx') for v in row] for row in cc[1:]],[74*mm,30*mm,30*mm,30*mm]),Spacer(1,4),P('6.2 Preprocessing and training','h2x'),P('Images were resized to 224 x 224 pixels, converted to tensors, and normalized with ImageNet channel statistics. Training augmentation used horizontal flips (p=0.5), rotations up to 10 degrees, and mild brightness/contrast/saturation jitter (0.12). Training transforms were kept separate from tuning and test transforms. Batch size was 32.'),P('MobileNetV3-Small used ImageNet default pretrained weights and a replaced final layer with ten outputs. The loss was class-weighted cross-entropy, with weights proportional to the square root of inverse training frequency. The classifier head was trained up to five epochs with AdamW at 5e-4 learning rate and 1e-4 weight decay. The final four feature blocks were then fine-tuned for up to twelve more epochs at 2e-5 learning rate and 1e-4 weight decay. The run reached the 17-epoch cap; the best tuning macro-F1 checkpoint was epoch 15. The held-out test set was evaluated once after checkpoint selection.'),P('Training ran on CPU for approximately 351 seconds. At epoch 15, training accuracy was 81.75% and tuning accuracy 67.14%, a gap of about 14.6 percentage points. This indicates possible overfitting, but it is not a reliable estimate of future performance because the dataset and test split are small.'),PageBreak(),P('7. Prototype and Hardware Plan','h1x'),P('Reported available parts are Raspberry Pi 5, ESP32, L298N motor driver, chassis, DC motors/wheels, breadboard, and jumper wires. Planned purchases are an MLX90614/GY-906 temperature module, MAX30102 heart-rate/SpO2 module, and USB webcam. The supplied photograph shows a Raspberry Pi connected to a display running the DiagnoBot interface.')]
